00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,560
Statement versus question intonation. You may have learned at some point that

2
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:09,440
questions have a rising intonation. They do, but usually a question will step

3
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:15,060
upward until the very end where it takes one quick little downward step. A question

4
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:19,840
rises a little higher than a statement with the same intonation pattern. Here's

5
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:27,660
my car. Where's my car? Emotional or rhetorical question intonation. If you

6
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:31,460
know that your car is parked outside, however, and someone doesn't see it and

7
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:35,620
ask you where it is, you might think that it has been stolen, and your emotion will

8
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:40,460
show in your intonation as you repeat the question. As your feelings rise in an

9
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:47,200
emotional situation, your intonation rises up along with them. Where's my car? Why?

10
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:48,120
Is it gone?
